00:39:17.825 --> 00:39:18.805
interesting, Luciano.

1025
00:39:19.465 --> 00:39:22.626
How can we take this really cool topic and

1026
00:39:23.406 --> 00:39:23.947
summarize it?

1027
00:39:24.727 --> 00:39:26.767
Yeah, we are in the process of publishing an

1028
00:39:26.787 --> 00:39:29.208
entire article that goes deep dive into this.

1029
00:39:29.288 --> 00:39:31.089
So I'm just going to briefly mention what we're

1030
00:39:31.129 --> 00:39:33.150
talking about, and then we'll defer you to the

1031
00:39:33.210 --> 00:39:34.450
article if you want to deep dive.

1032
00:39:34.910 --> 00:39:36.731
But basically, one of the main problems that you

1033
00:39:36.791 --> 00:39:39.011
face when you try to integrate an LLM into

1034
00:39:39.051 --> 00:39:40.492
something programmatic is that

1035
00:39:41.032 --> 00:39:43.715
The LLM generates text, but what you want is

1036
00:39:43.775 --> 00:39:45.116
generally something more structured,

1037
00:39:45.156 --> 00:39:47.338
like a JSON object that you can parse and then

1038
00:39:47.378 --> 00:39:48.899
reuse into the rest of your code.

1039
00:39:49.440 --> 00:39:50.261
But there are problems.

1040
00:39:50.421 --> 00:39:53.403
You can tell the LLM to respond with a snippet

1041
00:39:53.483 --> 00:39:56.206
in JSON, and then the LLM might get a little

1042
00:39:56.226 --> 00:39:57.347
bit creative sometimes.

1043
00:39:57.367 --> 00:39:59.069
So sometimes it's just going to use markdown

1044
00:39:59.149 --> 00:40:00.670
fences where you have, I don't know,

1045
00:40:00.730 --> 00:40:03.393
backtick, backtick, JSON, then all the JSON

1046
00:40:03.433 --> 00:40:05.274
inside, and then backtick, backtick,

1047
00:40:05.314 --> 00:40:05.795
backtick.

1048
00:40:06.395 --> 00:40:08.877
And then you need to write code that can remove

