00:40:08.917 --> 00:40:10.999
the backticks and all the markdown wrapping and

1050
00:40:11.039 --> 00:40:12.920
just take the JSON and do a JSON parse.

1051
00:40:13.721 --> 00:40:16.363
Sometimes, even worse, it happens more rarely

1052
00:40:16.403 --> 00:40:18.404
with the more capable models, but I've still

1053
00:40:18.504 --> 00:40:18.864
seen it.

1054
00:40:19.205 --> 00:40:21.887
Sometimes the JSON that you get is not perfectly

1055
00:40:22.007 --> 00:40:22.567
compliant.

1056
00:40:23.128 --> 00:40:26.250
You might get a trailing comma, or even worse,

1057
00:40:26.270 --> 00:40:28.351
you might get fields that you didn't define

1058
00:40:28.511 --> 00:40:30.913
initially just because the LLM is getting creative.

1059
00:40:31.454 --> 00:40:33.235
So this is kind of a common problem.

1060
00:40:33.415 --> 00:40:35.017
Oh yeah, there is another interesting use case

1061
00:40:35.117 --> 00:40:37.439
where the LLM actually gives you multiple JSON

1062
00:40:37.459 --> 00:40:37.959
snippets.

1063
00:40:38.039 --> 00:40:39.441
So it's kind of reasoning and saying,

1064
00:40:39.781 --> 00:40:42.043
this was my first attempt, then I realized that

